  "description": "**Conversation Summary**\n\n1. **Request:** The column header in the Kanban/Sprint board had too many elements crammed into one row, leaving no space for the column title; secondary info (project, profiles) needed to move to its own row.\n2. **Analysis:** Reviewed the header markup \u2014 grip, status icon, project avatar, profile avatar group, count pill, title, cost, and two action buttons all competed inside a 256px column width.\n3. **Solution:** Split the header into two stacked rows \u2014 a primary row (grip, status icon, title, task count, cost, actions) and a conditional secondary row (assigned project + profile avatars).\n4. **Key detail:** The title was promoted to `text-sm font-semibold flex-1 min-w-0 truncate` with a native `title` tooltip, guaranteeing it always gets space; added a `columnProjectName` computed and fixed the mislabeled \"Add task\" button title.\n5. **Delivery:** One file change proposed \u2014 `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` \u2014 plus specs table, anti-patterns (count pill before title, fixed-width title, empty meta row), and an accessibility checklist.",
